 ### Blending-Based Rasterization (VoxelPipe Standard Mode)
-A sort-middle tile-based rasterization pipeline divided into coarse raster and fine raster stages. Coarse raster divides the grid into coarse tiles, performs triangle setup, and emits triangles overlapping each tile. Fine raster assigns each tile to a core, generates fragments, and performs blending in shared memory. Advantages include load balancing by breaking large triangles across multiple tiles and reduced expensive memory bandwidth by doing heavy-lifting in the upper memory hierarchy (shared memory) [S1].
