 ## Background
-VoxelPipe was introduced by researchers at NVIDIA [S1]. The source code is available at http://code.google.com/p/voxelpipe/ [S1]. It is used in real-time global illumination systems (AnonGI) to create a scene proxy for tracing incoherent rays, rebuilt every frame for dynamic geometry, materials, and lighting, running at over 50 FPS at 1024x1024 resolution [S1].
